# xavi-man

`xavi-man` replaces the old Xavi Textual/curses management interface with a Windows 3.11-inspired operations desktop.

## Surfaces

- Terminal: `cd /var/www/xavi && ./xavi-man`
- Web: `https://xavi.app/xavi-man/`
- Loopback service: `127.0.0.1:18731`

## Security model

The browser UI is not a shell. It exposes only the existing `StackManager` allowlisted operations. Public access is expected to be gated by ConcreteCMS v9 `auth_request` and admin membership. A separate five-minute HS256 JWT with `aud=xavi-man`, `admin=true`, and `xavi-man:control` scope is available for token-friendly clients.

All mutations require a dry-run preview followed by an explicit `APPLY` confirmation.
